        "Approved actions for this command-center Singapore routine:\n"
        "- APPROVED for this routine: let the deterministic background runner use its host-private Gmail and server configuration internally. Agents must not locate, read, or print those files.\n"
        "- APPROVED for this routine: update or retire an existing private server-list entry only from a verified operator instruction or trusted credential-change email; reactivate a tombstone only from explicit reactivation instruction. Never auto-create an unknown entry. An explicit request for a brand-new Singapore interface is cataloged for the gateway's ticket-only path without writing server configuration.\n"
        "- APPROVED for this Singapore routine only: send exactly one Zoom Team Chat message to the verified Julio direct recipient when true non-submission dates are present.\n"
        "- APPROVED for this routine: mark only the source non-submission messages read after exact Julio Zoom message-ID, body, sender-email, and configured-recipient-email readback succeeds and the verified delivery coverage is durably recorded.\n"
        "- APPROVED for this routine: mark pure zero-sales notices read with per-message Gmail readback because they require store-owner confirmation, not Nova action.\n"
        "- APPROVED for this routine: catalog every automated upload outcome first, then mark authentication-failure sources read with per-message Gmail readback. Retired/deactivated sources are acknowledged and silently ignored. No upload, status, authentication, transfer, remediation, existing-configuration, or reactivation outcome may be gated on or routed to Salesforce or Needs Review.\n"
        "- Existing interfaces may be retired automatically only after 90 observed days with no verified successful submission and no verified customer resubmission/configuration/reactivation contact. Missing evidence fails closed and does not retire anything.\n"
        "- Send only one compact sanitized success/partial/failure line to Taylor's direct Agent Chat when active work occurred. Never include raw errors, identifiers, filenames, hostnames, usernames, paths, message bodies, tokens, or credentials. Do not send automatic customer replies or operational Salesforce tickets/review packets.\n"
        "- Only an explicit request to create/build/add/provision/onboard/set up a brand-new Singapore integration/interface may enter the gateway's Salesforce ticket path. A known retired interface remains silent unless explicitly reactivated; reactivation itself is background-service work and not a ticket.\n"
        "- Do not launch, rebuild, repair, or duplicate the desktop uploader. Use only the established headless FTP/SFTP modules.\n"
        "- The operator's verified instruction is the authorization; do not require a magic word or a second confirmation. Never initiate unrelated writes without an operator instruction.\n\n"
        "Critical filters:\n"
        "- Include only emails/items that report non-submission or missing submission dates for the Singapore FTP process.\n"
        "- Exclude zero-sales items from the Julio message and Darius notifications. Mark pure zero-sales source messages read with exact Gmail readback.\n"
        "- Exclude and disregard sales-verification / sales verification items. Do not message Julio about those and do not notify Darius about them.\n"
        "- Dedupe by machine, location, and date before composing the Julio message.\n\n"
        "The deterministic runner resolves approved parser modules and private credential/server state internally. Never request, reveal, or copy its local paths, filenames, secret values, or raw diagnostics. Server changes use the dedicated atomic patch operation and report field names only.\n\n"
        "Zoom message handling:\n"
        f"- Recipient hint: {recipient_hint or 'Julio'}.\n"
        "- Reuse the existing Support Dashboard Calls Server-to-Server OAuth app with the explicit configured sender. Use only the exact active contact email in `ZOOM_SINGAPORE_JULIO_CONTACT`; never use `me`, General OAuth, a name, user ID, guessed contact, group, or channel.\n"
        "- Send at most one source-safe Zoom Team Chat batch of no more than 600 characters for this run, and only if there is at least one true non-submission date that still needs Julio to resend. Never split rows linked to one source email across batches.\n"
        "- Before the provider call, atomically persist the exact source IDs, machine/date rows, rendered body, and body hash in the durable outbox. Reconcile an unfinished outbox before another send. Persist exact message-ID/body/sender-email/configured-recipient-email verification before Gmail mutation; leave overflow sources unread for later five-minute continuation cycles.\n"
        "- The message should be concise, include the greeting, and use Darius's tenant/date shorthand. Use this shape:\n"
